{"name":"Clove Dye","hex":"#a96232","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clove","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very pungent aromatic spice, the unexpanded flower bud of the clove tree.","A clove tree, of the species Syzygium aromaticum (syn. Caryophyllus aromaticus), native to the Moluccas (Indonesian islands), which produces the spice."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of the small bulbs that make up the large, compound bulb in garlic, shallots, or similar plants.","A segment or natural division of a fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clove"},{"term":"dye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colorant, especially one that has an affinity to the substrate to which it is applied.","Any hue or color."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To colour with dye, or as if with dye."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clove","blocks":[{"text":"Cloves are the aromatic flower buds of a tree in the family Myrtaceae, Syzygium aromaticum. They are native to the Maluku Islands, or Moluccas, in Indonesia, and are commonly used as a spice, flavoring, or fragrance in consumer products, such as toothpaste, soaps, or cosmetics. Freshly harvested cloves are available throughout the year owing to different harvest seasons across various countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Syzygium_aromaticum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-030.jpg/330px-Syzygium_aromaticum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-030.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clove","wikidata":"Q26736"},{"title":"Dye","blocks":[{"text":"A dye is a colored substance that is soluble in some solvent; by contrast pigments are insoluble or nearly so in all solvents. Because of their solubility, dyes can chemically bind to the material they color. Dye is generally applied in an aqueous solution and may require a mordant to improve the fastness of the dye on the fiber."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2019-11-22_Some_of_the_dyes_made_at_De_Kat.jpg/330px-2019-11-22_Some_of_the_dyes_made_at_De_Kat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dye","wikidata":"Q189720"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/ClovesDried.jpg/500px-ClovesDried.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/ClovesDried.jpg/500px-ClovesDried.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dried cloves","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClovesDried.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG/500px-The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG/1280px-The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG/500px-The_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clove tree flowerbuds","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_flowers_of_clove_tree_in_Pemba_island.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Seasonal_clove_buds_drying_on_Pemba1.jpg/500px-Seasonal_clove_buds_drying_on_Pemba1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Seasonal_clove_buds_drying_on_Pemba1.jpg/500px-Season